So, it's been 5 years since the latest nethack release.  

The Devteam is hard to communicate with.

There may never be another version.

But that in itself isn't a disaster. 

If we look at Nethack as a _Finished_ game, it's a pretty 
darn good one.  The most recent version holds the attention 
of many players for years - something I can say of no 
commercial games of which I know. 

I was struck by the length and vehemence of this thread, 
when the OP didn't even mention anything s/he wanted added 
or changed.  This wasn't a feature request, or a change 
request, or a bug report, or any other reason to have a 
new version.  This was just ... an expectation that there 
should be a new version.  That's all.   

Ladies & gentlemen, we should ask ourselves: _WHY_ get 
hung up on whether there's a new version or not?  Just 
expecting that there should be one isn't a reason for 
one to exist.  

There are a few outstanding bugs.  Enough, I suppose, to 
justify a second-point (3.4.4) release.  Anything else? 
Or is nethack finally complete?

If, fifteen years from now, 3.4.3 is still the current 
version, do we lose anything?  The game has already advanced 
to the point where virtually all players, even players that 
have been playing the same version for five years and played 
other versions for seven years before that, are still in their 
learning curve.  A new version would keep them in their 
learning curve, but that's where they are anyway.  They don't 
need a new version to get a version they don't know everything
about. 

Nobody needs a new version of chess.  You can fiddle with the 
UI and graphics all you want, but chess is a great game with 
its current rules.  You can literally spend a lifetime mastering
it.  So is the current (perhaps the last) version of nethack. 

Maybe we should start looking at the possibility that 
nethack exists as it is, and will continue to exist as it 
is into the indefinite future, and that that isn't necessarily
a disaster.  

